    "answer": {
      "short": "$r=\\dfrac{24s}{t}$.\n\nCompleted rows, from left to right:\n\n$r$: $24,\\ 12,\\ 24,\\ 48,\\ 4$.\n\n$s$: $1,\\ 1,\\ 2,\\ 2,\\ 2$.\n\n$t$: $1,\\ 2,\\ 2,\\ 1,\\ 12$.",
      "worked": "Write $r=\\dfrac{ks}{t}$. Using the first column:\n$$\\begin{align*}24&=\\frac{k\\times1}{1}\\\\k&=24\\\\r&=\\frac{24s}{t}\\end{align*}$$\nFor the second column:\n$$\\begin{align*}12&=\\frac{24s}{2}\\\\s&=1\\end{align*}$$\nFor the third column:\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{24\\times2}{2}\\\\r&=24\\end{align*}$$\nFor the fourth column:\n$$\\begin{align*}48&=\\frac{24s}{1}\\\\s&=2\\end{align*}$$\nFor the fifth column:\n$$\\begin{align*}4&=\\frac{24\\times2}{t}\\\\4t&=48\\\\t&=12\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
